{"event": "token", "client_s": 28.886, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:56.937Z", "t_ms": 8528, "delta": " token called `Retrieve` [C1, C2, C5]:\n\n* **Segment-Level Decision:** Given"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 29.148, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:57.196Z", "t_ms": 8787, "delta": " the input prompt $x$ and the preceding generated text $y_{<t}$, the generator language model decodes a "}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 29.332, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:57.382Z", "t_ms": 8973, "delta": "`Retrieve` token at the start of each output segment to assess whether factual grounding is required [C2, C3,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 29.627, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:57.677Z", "t_ms": 9268, "delta": " C7].\n* **Token Values:** The `Retrieve` token can take values such as `{yes, no, continue}` [C"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 29.862, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:57.912Z", "t_ms": 9504, "delta": "2]. A `yes` indicates retrieval is necessary, `no` indicates the sequence does not require factual grounding or would"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 30.093, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:58.144Z", "t_ms": 9735, "delta": " not benefit from retrieval, and `continue` indicates the model can continue using previously retrieved evidence [C7].\n* **Inference Mechanisms ("}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 30.365, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:58.416Z", "t_ms": 10007, "delta": "Hard vs. Soft/Threshold Control):** \n  * In standard greedy or hard control, retrieval is triggered if"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 30.551, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:58.602Z", "t_ms": 10193, "delta": " `Retrieve == Yes` [C2, C3, C5]. If `no`, the model generates the segment"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 30.712, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:58.762Z", "t_ms": 10354, "delta": " without retrieving, behaving like a standard LM [C2, C3].\n  * Alternatively, Self-RAG supports"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 30.994, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:59.036Z", "t_ms": 10627, "delta": " adaptive retrieval via a tunable threshold: retrieval is triggered if the generation probability of `Retrieve = Yes`, normalized over all output tokens"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 31.3, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:59.316Z", "t_ms": 10908, "delta": " in `Retrieve`, exceeds a designated threshold [C5]. This allows tailoring the retrieval frequency to different task demands, such as retrieving"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 31.39, "data": {"request_id": "69c41a599c24", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:09:59.440Z", "t_ms": 11031, "delta": " more frequently for fact-heavy tasks or less frequently for creative tasks [C5]."}}
